<code_editing_rules>

<guiding_principles>
- Clarity and Reuse: Ensure all modules, services, and components are modular and reusable across the large codebase. Refactor duplicated logic or UI patterns into shared modules or components.
- Consistency: Maintain strict adherence to a unified design and code convention system—including consistent use of color tokens, typography, spacing, component patterns (in the frontend), and API schemas (in the backend).
- Simplicity: Favor small, focused components, services, and endpoints. Avoid unnecessary complexity in business logic, state handling, or styling.
- Demo-Oriented: Structure the refactor to enable rapid prototyping and clear demonstration of complex capabilities like OpenAI Agent SDK integrations or Pydantic AI Agents SDK, streaming, multi-turn conversations, and tool or plugin integrations.
- Visual Quality: Achieve a high visual quality bar following shared OSS guidelines (proper spacing, padding, accessible states, etc.) across both frontend (React/Next.js/Vite) and API documentation (FastAPI).
</guiding_principles>

<refactor_stack_defaults>
- Model: All model usage must leverage gpt-5 (as this is the most powerful model available to us, much better than gpt-4o, or gpt-4-turbo)
- Backend: FastAPI (Python, using Pydantic 2.11 for data models and validation, or with the Pydantic Agent SDK)
- Frontend: Next.js (TypeScript), React, Vite (when required for client-side apps)
- Styling: TailwindCSS
- UI Components: shadcn/ui
- Icons: Lucide
- State Management: Zustand (for React apps)
- Directory Structure:
```
/backend
  /api                  # FastAPI endpoints
  /agents               # OpenAI agent SDK pipelining
  /schemas              # Pydantic 2.11 models and validation
  /utils                # Shared backend utilities
/frontend
  /src
    /app                # Next.js, React or Vite page routes
    /components         # UI building blocks
    /hooks              # Reusable React hooks
    /lib                # Shared utilities (fetchers, helpers)
    /stores             # Zustand stores
    /types              # Shared TypeScript types
    /styles             # Tailwind config
```
</refactor_stack_defaults>

<below only for frontend, else ignore>

<ui_ux_best_practices>
- Visual Hierarchy: Limit typography to 4–5 font sizes/weights for consistent hierarchy; use `text-xs` for captions and annotations; use `text-xl` only for hero sections/major headings (which can be appropriately sized for the context)
- Color Usage: Use a single neutral base (e.g., `zinc`) and up to 2 accent colors consistently across frontend modules.
- Spacing and Layout: Use multiples of 4 for padding/margin. In long content/streaming flows, use fixed-height containers with internal scrolling.
- Voice-Only App: The application must not allow any user interaction via screen, keyboard, or mouse—voice is the only permitted input modality.
- Accessibility: Use semantic HTML and ARIA roles where appropriate in React/Next.js; leverage accessible FastAPI documentation and schemas; favor Radix/shadcn prebuilt components.
</ui_ux_best_practices>

